# Web App — Mantine Over HTML

**Source of truth:** `apps/web-app/docs/mantine-component-guide.md`

## Non-negotiable rules

- **Prefer Mantine over plain HTML.** Use Mantine components instead of raw HTML tags wherever a Mantine equivalent exists.
- **NO unnecessary HTML tags.** Do not use `<div>`, `<p>`, `<h1>`–`<h6>` when a Mantine component covers the use case.
- **Only use HTML when necessary:** `<section>`, `<form>`, `<a>`, `<ul>`, `<li>`, semantic landmarks, or when Mantine has no equivalent.

## Mapping

- Container/generic wrapper → `Box` (`@mantine/core`)
- Vertical layout → `Stack` (`@mantine/core`)
- Horizontal layout → `Group` (`@mantine/core`)
- Headings (`h1`–`h6`) → `Title order={n}` (`@mantine/core`)
- Paragraph / body text → `Text` from `@/components` (project wrapper)
- Button → project `Button` from `@/components`

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG
<div className="flex flex-col gap-4">
  <h2 className="text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary">Title</h2>
  <p className="text-text-secondary">Description</p>
</div>

// ✅ CORRECT
import { Stack, Title } from "@mantine/core";
import { Text } from "@/components";

<Stack gap="md">
  <Title order={2} className="text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary">Title</Title>
  <Text className="text-text-secondary">Description</Text>
</Stack>
```

## Before writing any web component

1. Read `apps/web-app/docs/mantine-component-guide.md` for the full guide and examples.
2. Replace every `<div>`, `<p>`, `<h*>` with the correct Mantine component before finishing.
3. `<section>` is acceptable for semantic page sections — wrap its inner content with Mantine layout components.
